# Evidence payloads are provenance artifacts. Their bytes must match the SHA-256
# recorded in the SOURCE-RECORD.md alongside them, so they must never be subject
# to line-ending conversion.
#
# Why this file exists (found 2026-08-29): with no .gitattributes and Windows
# core.autocrlf active, checked-out evidence did not match its own recorded
# hashes. Indiana's WZDx registry copy recorded 19,480 bytes / ea7ff56c... but
# hashed 2e9150b1... on disk at 19,522 bytes, and its cctv.xml recorded 759,718
# bytes but was 777,626 on disk. The recorded values were correct all along --
# they match git's stored blob and a fresh fetch -- but anyone verifying a hash
# against a Windows working copy would have seen a mismatch and reasonably
# concluded the evidence had been altered.
sources/**                                 -text
data/states/*/events/**                    -text
data/states/*/sensor-observations/**       -text
data/states/*/media-streams/**             -text
data/states/*/documents-static-datasets/** -text
